---
// Egypt — Section 11: "1922"
// The most cinematic moment. Progressive reveal of Howard Carter's discovery.
---

<section
  class="relative flex min-h-svh items-center overflow-hidden bg-[var(--egypt-obsidian)]"
  aria-labelledby="discovery-heading"
>
  <!-- Golden light stripe from center -->
  <div
    class="pointer-events-none absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center"
    aria-hidden="true"
  >
    <div
      class="h-full w-px bg-gradient-to-b from-transparent via-[var(--egypt-gold)]/20 to-transparent"
    >
    </div>
  </div>

  <div
    class="relative mx-auto w-full max-w-landing px-container-x py-section sm:px-8 xl:px-14"
  >
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl text-center">
      <!-- Progressive reveal sequence -->
      <p
        class="font-display text-[clamp(5rem,12vw,12rem)] uppercase leading-none tracking-wider text-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
        data-discovery
        aria-label="1922"
      >
        1922
      </p>

      <p
        class="mt-8 font-display text-headline-2 uppercase tracking-wider text-white"
        data-discovery
      >
        Howard Carter
      </p>

      <p
        class="mt-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/50"
        data-discovery
      >
        Valley of the Kings
      </p>

      <div
        class="mx-auto my-12 h-px w-24 bg-[var(--egypt-gold)]/30"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
      </div>

      <p
        class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/70 italic"
        data-discovery
      >
        After more than 3,000 years, the seal was broken.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="mt-12" data-discovery>
        <p class="text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/50 italic">
          "Can you see anything?"
        </p>
        <p
          class="mt-6 font-display text-headline-3 uppercase leading-snug tracking-wide text-[var(--egypt-gold)]"
        >
          "Yes, wonderful things."
        </p>
        <cite class="mt-4 block text-xs text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/40 not-italic">
          — Lord Carnarvon and Howard Carter, November 26, 1922
        </cite>
      </blockquote>

      <p
        class="mt-12 max-w-md mx-auto text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--egypt-sand)]/60"
        data-discovery
      >
        Inside the sealed chamber lay the most complete royal tomb ever found.
        Over five thousand artifacts. The golden mask. The nested coffins. Three
        millennia of silence, broken by a single candle.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
